WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.037
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book two.

2
00:00:05.337 --> 00:00:08.688
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.988 --> 00:00:14.114
Unit four: Seasons & Climate. In this unit, you will compare seasons and weather.

4
00:00:15.117 --> 00:00:15.978
Spring.

5
00:00:16.678 --> 00:00:19.874
Spring means the season after winter, when flowers grow.

6
00:00:20.174 --> 00:00:21.686
Flowers bloom in spring.

7
00:00:22.386 --> 00:00:25.328
Your turn. Say: Spring.

8
00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:28.890
Spring.

9
00:00:29.883 --> 00:00:30.710
Summer.

10
00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:33.584
Summer means the hottest season of the year.

11
00:00:33.884 --> 00:00:36.162
Summer is very hot in Japan.

12
00:00:36.862 --> 00:00:39.027
Your turn. Say: Summer.

13
00:00:41.727 --> 00:00:42.542
Summer.

14
00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:44.389
Autumn.

15
00:00:45.089 --> 00:00:47.727
Autumn means the season when leaves fall.

16
00:00:48.027 --> 00:00:49.794
Leaves turn orange in autumn.

17
00:00:50.494 --> 00:00:52.508
Your turn. Say: Autumn.

18
00:00:55.208 --> 00:00:56.011
Autumn.

19
00:00:57.017 --> 00:00:57.913
Winter.

20
00:00:58.613 --> 00:01:01.205
Winter means the coldest season of the year.

21
00:01:01.505 --> 00:01:03.423
It snows in winter in Korea.

22
00:01:04.123 --> 00:01:06.776
Your turn. Say: Winter.

23
00:01:09.476 --> 00:01:10.384
Winter.

24
00:01:11.383 --> 00:01:12.257
Temperature.

25
00:01:12.957 --> 00:01:15.595
Temperature means how hot or cold something is.

26
00:01:15.895 --> 00:01:17.720
The temperature is thirty degrees.

27
00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:21.073
Your turn. Say: Temperature.

28
00:01:23.773 --> 00:01:24.669
Temperature.

29
00:01:25.683 --> 00:01:26.475
Humid.

30
00:01:27.175 --> 00:01:29.187
Humid means hot and wet in the air.

31
00:01:29.487 --> 00:01:31.707
April is very humid in Cambodia.

32
00:01:32.407 --> 00:01:34.699
Your turn. Say: Humid.

33
00:01:37.399 --> 00:01:38.122
Humid.

34
00:01:39.117 --> 00:01:40.187
Monsoon.

35
00:01:40.887 --> 00:01:43.607
Monsoon means the season of heavy rain in Asia.

36
00:01:43.907 --> 00:01:45.953
The monsoon brings rain for the rice.

37
00:01:46.653 --> 00:01:49.317
Your turn. Say: Monsoon.

38
00:01:52.017 --> 00:01:52.925
Monsoon.

39
00:01:53.917 --> 00:01:54.593
Drought.

40
00:01:55.293 --> 00:01:57.432
Drought means a long time with no rain.

41
00:01:57.732 --> 00:01:59.859
The drought made the rice fields dry.

42
00:02:00.559 --> 00:02:02.805
Your turn. Say: Drought.

43
00:02:05.505 --> 00:02:06.169
Drought.

44
00:02:07.183 --> 00:02:08.138
Forecast.

45
00:02:08.838 --> 00:02:11.430
Forecast means a report about the weather to come.

46
00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:13.381
The forecast says it will rain.

47
00:02:14.081 --> 00:02:16.455
Your turn. Say: Forecast.

48
00:02:19.155 --> 00:02:20.144
Forecast.

49
00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:22.070
Thermometer.

50
00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:26.023
Thermometer means a tool that measures temperature.

51
00:02:26.323 --> 00:02:28.822
The thermometer shows 35 degrees.

52
00:02:29.522 --> 00:02:32.616
Your turn. Say: Thermometer.

53
00:02:35.316 --> 00:02:36.479
Thermometer.

54
00:02:37.483 --> 00:02:38.438
Breeze.

55
00:02:39.138 --> 00:02:41.532
Breeze means a light, gentle wind.

56
00:02:41.832 --> 00:02:43.809
A cool breeze comes from the sea.

57
00:02:44.509 --> 00:02:46.662
Your turn. Say: Breeze.

58
00:02:49.362 --> 00:02:50.247
Breeze.

59
00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:52.228
Storm warning.

60
00:02:52.928 --> 00:02:55.914
Storm warning means a message that a dangerous storm is coming.

61
00:02:56.214 --> 00:02:58.121
There's a storm warning for tonight.

62
00:02:58.821 --> 00:03:02.147
Your turn. Say: Storm warning.

63
00:03:04.847 --> 00:03:05.836
Storm warning.

64
00:03:06.850 --> 00:03:08.966
Now let's listen to a conversation.

65
00:03:09.266 --> 00:03:12.798
Sreypich, Cambodia has a wet season and a dry season, right?

66
00:03:14.083 --> 00:03:16.921
Yes. The monsoon brings heavy rain.

67
00:03:18.217 --> 00:03:21.821
In America, we have four seasons. Summer is hotter than winter.

68
00:03:23.117 --> 00:03:24.803
Is winter colder than here?

69
00:03:26.117 --> 00:03:28.839
Much colder! Sometimes it snows.

70
00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:32.756
Wow! I'd like to see snow one day.

71
00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:37.303
Grammar focus: Comparative adjectives.

72
00:03:37.603 --> 00:03:39.266
Summer is hotter than winter.

73
00:03:39.566 --> 00:03:44.341
For hot, big and wet, double the last letter: hotter, bigger, wetter.

74
00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:48.176
Now read and listen. Four Seasons and Two.

75
00:03:48.476 --> 00:03:52.438
Many countries have four seasons: spring, summer, autumn and winter.

76
00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:57.921
In summer, the temperature is high, and in winter, the weather turns cold.

77
00:03:59.217 --> 00:04:02.273
Cambodia has a dry season and a wet season instead.

78
00:04:03.583 --> 00:04:06.744
The monsoon brings rain, but sometimes there is a drought.

79
00:04:08.050 --> 00:04:10.653
Always check the forecast for storm warnings!

80
00:04:11.950 --> 00:04:14.335
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

81
00:04:14.635 --> 00:04:16.449
Summer is blank than winter.

82
00:04:16.749 --> 00:04:20.124
A, hotter. B, hoter. C, more hot.

83
00:04:24.117 --> 00:04:25.814
The answer is A: hotter.

84
00:04:27.317 --> 00:04:29.514
A long time with no rain is a blank.

85
00:04:29.814 --> 00:04:33.003
A, drought. B, monsoon. C, breeze.

86
00:04:37.017 --> 00:04:38.633
The answer is A: drought.

87
00:04:40.117 --> 00:04:43.103
A tool that measures temperature is a blank.

88
00:04:43.403 --> 00:04:48.148
A, thermometer. B, forecast. C, monsoon.

89
00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:54.382
The answer is A: thermometer.

90
00:04:55.883 --> 00:04:59.581
Now it's your turn to speak. Which season do you like best and why?

91
00:05:04.881 --> 00:05:09.063
I like the cool season best because it is less humid and cooler than April.

92
00:05:09.363 --> 00:05:11.153
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

93
00:05:12.150 --> 00:05:16.381
Great work today! You learned twelve new words and comparative adjectives.

94
00:05:16.681 --> 00:05:21.481
Today's value is adaptability. Be ready for rain or sun and change your plans.

95
00:05:21.781 --> 00:05:24.248
See you in Unit five. Goodbye!

96
00:05:24.548 --> 00:05:27.316
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

